# Home Backup Ignore Configuration
# Gitignore-style patterns for rsync --exclude-from (see docs/backup-principles.md
# for the principles behind every rule and the exact pattern semantics).
#
# Copy to config/home-backup-ignore and adapt to your machine.
# Decide per entry: is this data (rarity tiers 1-3 → keep) or is it
# rebuildable/re-obtainable (tiers 4-5 → exclude)?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tier 5: caches
# Auto-regenerated volatile data (tier 5)
.cache/
.thumbnails/
.gvfs/
.local/share/Trash/
.fontconfig/

# Flatpak per-app caches (tier 5)
.var/app/*/cache/

# Browser caches (tier 5; profile data itself stays — bookmarks and passwords
# are tier 1)
.cache/google-chrome/
.cache/chromium/
.cache/mozilla/
.mozilla/firefox/*/cache*/
.var/app/*/cache/

# AI tool caches and model weights (tier 4 — re-download)
.ollama/
.claude/
.gemini/

# ------------------------------------------------- tier 4: package caches/stores
# NOTE: Back up containers manually using 'podman save' / 'podman export'
.local/share/containers/storage/
.config/containers/

# Dev tool caches (tier 4 — refetch on demand)
.npm/_cacache/
.npm/_npx/
.cargo/registry/
.cargo/git/
.gradle/caches/
.m2/repository/
.local/share/JetBrains/
.vscode/extensions/
.local/share/pnpm/store/

# Tool runtimes — reinstall with the tool's own installer (tier 4)
.local/share/mise/installs/
.local/share/mise/downloads/
.rustup/
.local/share/uv/
.pub-cache/
.dart-tool/
.dartServer/
.flutter-devtools/
.local/share/venvs/
.local/share/pipx/

# Editor plugin state, re-install via package manager (tier 4)
.emacs.d/elpa/
.emacs.d/straight/build/
.emacs.d/straight/repos/
.local/share/nvim/

# ------------------------------------------------ tier 4: bulk re-obtainable data
# SDKs / IDEs / VM images — downloadable or rebuildable, huge (tier 4)
# sdks/
# applications/
# vms/

# Public datasets you can re-download (e.g. Kiwix ZIM dumps, torrent clients'
# download dirs) — tier 4
# documents/kiwix/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ scope: large dirs
# Large data directories managed in @data/@archive or by dedicated tools.
# These are personal choices — list yours here with a comment on where they
# are handled instead.
# downloads/
# music/
# videos/

# Project build artifacts and dependency caches (tier 4/5)
# Scoped to project roots so home-level state outside active repos is preserved.
projects/**/node_modules/
projects/**/__pycache__/
projects/**/.venv/
projects/**/.dart_tool/
projects/**/target/
projects/**/build/
projects/**/dist/
projects/**/.pytest_cache/
projects/**/.mypy_cache/

# Negation note: rsync does NOT re-include inside an excluded directory.
# To keep one subtree (e.g. Steam saves), exclude its siblings instead:
#   Steam/steamapps/
#   Steam/runtime/
#   ... rather than  Steam/  +  !Steam/userdata/   (which silently fails)
